{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1501492-exalted-mtg-cards","id":1501492,"title":"Exalted - MTG cards","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-01-27T16:11:18-08:00","id":1501492,"title":"Exalted - MTG cards","content":"Yay the forums are back! I can finally post these things I made during lockdown while bored.<br /> <br /> I'm terrible at homebrewing anything so I mostly took existing cards then changed the artwork, affects and flavour text. I tried to credit artists where possible.<br /> <br /> I tried to make the cards thematic and I'm aware that the powers aren't balanced perfectly. Like how Ligier is arguably stronger than Malfeas here, and I know that's not what Malfeas looks like etc.<br /> <br /> I also tried to design the cards around sets and tribes, as if they would be part of a real release for MTG.<br /> <br /> I started with the Yozi and matched the five primary ones to a 3 colour combination. So in the case of Malfeas, I went with Red/Green/Black, or Jund as it's otherwise known. For those who don't know, Jund as a colour combination is described as a world of pure freedom. Every animal can do whatever they want to do. There is no authority of Jund, and therefore the world has become crazy and wild. Since Jund lacks white and blue mana, there is no peace and thought. Instinct is the choice over control and deliberation&quot;. Not a perfect match but seemed close enough to me that it matched the flavour of Malfeas.<br /> <br /> Feedback is welcome <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <img width=\"194\" height=\"271\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/RGVop5y.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/RGVop5y.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.c