 <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1501492-exalted-mtg-cards?p=1502185#post1502185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fun stuff! I'm not going to argue over Jund themes, because what colors Malfeas is has more to do with where the effects you want to associate with him come from in the color pie - see sets like the new Phyrexia or the Eldrazi block for examples, and the secret lairs for what happens when you port other universes into Magic<br /> <br /> I might suggest that Yozi avatars, Incarna, Deathlords, 3rd circles and the like would be more interesting to port as Planeswalkers rather than creatures.</div> </div> </div> </div>Forgot I had posted these, thanks for the feedback <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> My intention was to make named exalted characters from the setting as Planeswalkers and if possible just rename the Planeswalker type as Exalted. Seeing as the fluff in the TCG is that you are a planeswalker and when you play one they're like your buddies coming to help but will peace out if they reach 0 loyalty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4612-solar-lantern","name":"Solar Lantern","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T08:17:36-07:00","id":1510792,"title":"","content":"Making Exalted mechanically identical to planeswalkers is what I would do, too. That essentially makes some spells into Charms, sorcery, or necromancy that you (the player) are using as an Exalt would.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}